# Airflow DAG-discovery ignore — scoped to this directory + subdirs.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Airflow scheduler's DAGS_FOLDER is the git-sync worktree root
# (/opt/airflow/dags-git/current); platform.git is committed under a
# top-level `platform/` dir, so this file lands at `current/platform/
# .airflowignore` and scopes Airflow's recursive scan to the platform
# subtree. The platform ships ZERO DAGs (DAGs are use-case-owned), so we
# prune every subtree that contains .py modules to stop the DagFileProcessor
# import-probing service code (which would raise spurious "Broken DAG"
# banners for modules whose deps aren't in the airflow image).
# Patterns are regexes (Airflow default DAG_IGNORE_FILE_SYNTAX=regexp),
# matched against each path relative to this directory.
components/
services/
scalability/
config/
